+# N — setup custom-node policy: allow every curated node, run install.py then requirements.txt (draft by main)
+
+## Owner request (2026-10-20 15:55, product authority)
+"When in setup wizard install custom nodes should be allow all even the security problem one and when install do this
+install.py -> requirements.txt."
+Context: earlier owner decisions this session — first-run setup installs ComfyUI-Manager and the selected curated nodes
+without consent pauses (review-step disclosure + Start setup = confirmation, NFR-SEC-3 first-run exception, package F);
+curated nodes install the latest default-branch commit (F2); Manager ticked / curated unticked by default (W).
+
+## Current behaviour (working copy through D4; D1 is being implemented concurrently and touches the same area)
+- Catalog `crates/infrastructure/src/environment/data/curated_nodes.json`: ComfyUI-PlagueKind-Nodes carries
+  `unavailable` ("Its repository tracks Python cache files (__pycache__), which the app refuses to install.") → the
+  wizard disables it, the backend refuses it (`curated_selection_invalid`).
+- Fresh Git content validation `crates/infrastructure/src/custom_nodes/tree.rs:199` `validate_fresh_git` =
+  `walk_files(git_node = true, reject_cache = true)`: tracked `__pycache__` anywhere → `UnsafeSource` (:149-151).
+  Containment refusals in the same walk (keep): path depth/bytes limits (:146-147), total bytes (:170-172), `.git`
+  only as a top-level directory of a Git node (:174-177), links/reparse points, name validation (`frame`).
+- D1 (in progress): on Windows, refuse NEW node content whose top-level folder holds a native image
+  (`.dll .exe .com .cpl .drv .ocx .scr .sys`), registry after extraction, Git via `ls-tree` before checkout and again
+  after — rationale: before exact-source consent, uv/git run with the staged node folder as cwd.
+- Setup decisions: `crates/application/src/custom_nodes/setup.rs:~156` forces `run_install_py = false`,
+  `remember_install_py = false`, `allow_source_builds = false`; F's `setup_review_decision` (execute.rs) synthesizes
+  `run_install_py: false`. The curated entry message carries `SETUP_HOOK_WARNING` ("install.py was not run …").
+- Commit order `crates/application/src/custom_nodes/workflow.rs:~805-869`: pin location → mark repair_required →
+  constraints → requirements install with the frozen preview plan (`package`) → reassert pins → **then** the hook
+  (`install.py`, only with `run_install_py`) → reassert pins → assert pins → verify_final → final snapshot (digest may
+  change only when the hook ran).
+- Reference installer (`docs/handoff/plans/m6-reference-data.md:33`): `git clone` default branch, then `install.py`
+  if present, then `requirements.txt`.
+
+## Proposed plan
+1. **Allow every curated node in first-run setup.** Remove `unavailable` from PlagueKind in the catalog (keep the
+   `unavailable` mechanism for future use). In setup (target `NodeTarget::Setup`) with the run's `third_party_consent`,
+   the content-policy refusals are not applied: tracked `__pycache__` (prepare uses a fresh-Git validation without
+   `reject_cache`) and D1's top-level native-image refusal (pre-consent rationale does not apply: consent precedes
+   every tool run in a consented first run). Containment refusals stay everywhere (links/reparse points, path limits,
+   size limit, `.git` placement, name validation). Each relaxed finding becomes a plan warning, logged as
+   "{name}: {warning} (acknowledged on the setup review page)." (F already logs and acknowledges warnings).
+   The Custom Nodes page and non-consented setup keep every refusal.
+2. **install.py then requirements.txt in setup.** With `third_party_consent`, the synthesized setup decision sets
+   `run_install_py = review.has_install_py` (still `remember_install_py = false`, `allow_source_builds = false`);
+   `commit_for_setup_held` stops forcing `run_install_py = false` when the run carries the consent. The commit order
+   for a decision with `run_install_py` becomes: pin location → repair_required → constraints → **hook (install.py)**
+   → reassert pins → **requirements install** (frozen preview plan) → reassert → assert pins → verify_final →
+   final snapshot (digest refreshed because the hook ran). Question: setup-only or every install (Custom Nodes page
+   with an approved install.py too)?
+3. UI/docs copy: the review disclosure no longer says "never runs install.py scripts" — new text: "…Setup installs the
+   latest commit of each repository's default branch, runs each node's install.py and then its requirements.txt, and
+   does not ask again. Clicking Start setup confirms this."; wizard curated copy; PlagueKind selectable;
+   `SETUP_HOOK_WARNING` only when install.py was NOT run; DOCUMENTATION, REQUIREMENTS NFR-SEC-3 / FR-SETUP-9 /
+   FR-NODE-4 notes (owner decision 2026-10-20).
+4. Tests: catalog (no unavailable entry), setup prepare accepts a tracked `__pycache__` / root native image only with
+   consent (warning recorded) and refuses links/limits regardless; refusal unchanged for the Custom Nodes page;
+   auto decision sets `run_install_py` iff `has_install_py`; commit order hook → requirements (recorded call order),
+   pins reasserted after each; hook failure → step failure as today; final digest refresh after hook.
+
+## Owner follow-ups (2026-10-20 16:00, answered)
+- "Apply it to custom nodes page install too" → clarified (AskUserQuestion): **order only**. The general node workflow
+  (Custom Nodes page installs/updates with an approved install.py, and setup) runs install.py FIRST, then
+  requirements.txt. The page keeps its per-plan review/consent and keeps every content-policy refusal (tracked
+  `__pycache__`, D1 top-level native images); only consented first-run setup relaxes them.
+- Question 2 below is therefore decided: the order change applies to the general workflow.
+
+## Questions for the advisor
+1. Exact boundary between "content policy" (relaxed in consented setup) and "containment" (never relaxed) — confirm or
+   correct the list, incl. how D1's refusal is bypassed for consented setup without weakening the Custom Nodes page.
+2. Order change scope: setup-only, or the general node workflow too (owner said "when install do this
+   install.py -> requirements.txt" in the setup-wizard context; ComfyUI-Manager itself runs requirements first)?
+3. install.py runs before requirements: is the pinned-package protection still sound (hook may pip-install anything;
+   reassert after the hook, the frozen requirement plan afterwards, final assert)? Any change needed to the preview
+   (requirements previewed before the hook may be stale after it)?
+4. allow_source_builds stays false (owner did not ask) — agree?
+5. Any user-only question left?
